# Security

- Platform credentials, HMAC signing, tokens, and secret configuration are server-only; browser code never calls Platform.
- Never expose secrets through `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`, browser bundles, responses, fixtures, screenshots, or source control.
- Never log JWTs, cookies, API secrets, HMAC signatures, passwords, payment credentials, or other sensitive values.
- Derive player identity from the authenticated session instead of browser input whenever possible.
- Validate untrusted input and external responses with Zod; reject unexpected data.
- Return stable, safe errors without raw upstream payloads, stack traces, or sensitive context.
- Tests use fakes only: no production credentials, and CI never calls Platform stage.
- Stop for human approval before changing authentication, authorization, cookies, secret handling, payments, or other security-sensitive architecture.
